{"content":[{"c":["HAZEROTH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Camp of the Israelites during their wanderings in the desert. It was the third camp from Mt Sinai (",{"href":"?bref=Num.11.35","r":"Num.11.35","rawR":"Num.11.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.11.35","value":"Num.11.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 11:35"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.12.16","r":"Num.12.16","rawR":"Num.12.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.12.16","value":"Num.12.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.33.17-18","r":"Num.33.17-18","rawR":"Num.33.17-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.33.17-18","value":"Num.33.17-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"33:17-18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.1.1","r":"Deut.1.1","rawR":"Deut.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.1.1","value":"Deut.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 1:1"},"). Here Miriam and Aaron spoke against Moses for marrying a Cushite woman and questioned whether God spoke only through Moses (",{"href":"?bref=Num.12.1-2","r":"Num.12.1-2","rawR":"Num.12.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.12.1-2","value":"Num.12.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 12:1-2"},"). The site is probably modern ‘Ain Khadra, about 30 miles (48 kilometers) northeast of Jebel Musa."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Wilderness Wanderings"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Hazeroth","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 11:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.11.35","rawQueryValue":"Num.11.35","sourceRefExact":"Num.11.35"},{"anchorText":"12:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.12.16","rawQueryValue":"Num.12.16","sourceRefExact":"Num.12.16"},{"anchorText":"33:17-18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.33.17-18","rawQueryValue":"Num.33.17-18","sourceRefExact":"Num.33.17-18"},{"anchorText":"Dt 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.1.1","rawQueryValue":"Deut.1.1","sourceRefExact":"Deut.1.1"},{"anchorText":"Nm 12:1-2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.12.1-2","rawQueryValue":"Num.12.1-2","sourceRefExact":"Num.12.1-2"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a0aeb009f9ec2d97f63a387672b06a9d661ec0c2859ae1f396dc843481382884","sourceItemName":"Hazeroth","sourceItemOrder":184,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Hazeroth","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hazeroth","title":"Hazeroth","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}